  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• To prepare the ingredients, peel and crush the garlic, and peel and grate the ginger. Cut the tofu into 1 cm thick strips, the Asian greens into 3 cm lengths, and the spring onions into 2 cm lengths. Trim the sugar snap peas, slice the chilli, and pick the coriander leaves."
    },
    {
      "text": "• Bring a large pot of salted water to the boil. Add the noodles and cook according to the packet directions. Refresh under cold water. Drain."
    },
    {
      "text": "• Combine the hoisin sauce, soy sauce, half of the vegetable oil, garlic, ginger and brown sugar."
    },
    {
      "text": "• Heat the remaining vegetable oil in a large wok or frying pan over medium-high heat. Add the tofu and cook, turning, for 1-2 minutes, or until the tofu is golden. Remove from the pan."
    },
    {
      "text": "• Add a dash of oil to the same wok or frying pan and add the Asian greens, sugar snap peas, spring onion, half of the chilli, and a splash of water. Cook, stirring, for 1-2 minutes. Add the hoisin sauce mixture, tofu and noodles and cook, tossing until everything is heated through. Remove from the heat and stir through the remaining chilli and coriander."
    },
    {
      "text": "• To serve, divide the saucy tofu noodles between plates."
    }
  ]
